# Virtual machine integration.
#
# VirtualBox: Debian 13 (trixie) no longer ships virtualbox-guest-utils,
# virtualbox-guest-x11 or virtualbox-guest-dkms in stable. The two userspace
# packages come from unstable/contrib through debian/archives/velcora-contrib.*
# (strictly pinned; the source and pin are removed before the image is made).
# They use the kernel's in-tree vboxguest/vboxsf/vboxvideo modules, so no
# out-of-tree module build is needed.
#
# The Guest Additions disc can still be used to update the tools at runtime;
# see velcora-install-guest-additions.
virtualbox-guest-utils
virtualbox-guest-x11

# Build prerequisites kept for the on-demand Guest Additions installer.
build-essential
dkms
linux-headers-amd64
perl
bzip2

# QEMU/KVM and SPICE integration.
qemu-guest-agent
spice-vdagent
